

#### 4.3.148 Formulas for Solution of Plane Triangles

In a triangle with angles \(A\), \(B\) and \(C\) and sides opposite \(a\), \(b\) and \(c\) respectively,

\[\frac{a}{\sin\ A} = \frac{b}{\sin\ B} = \frac{c}{\sin\ C}\]

\[\cos\ A = \frac{c^{2} + b^{2} - a^{2}}{2bc}\]

\[a = b\ \cos\ C + c\ \cos\ B\]

\[\frac{a + b}{a - b} = \frac{\tan\ \frac{1}{2}(A + B)}{\tan\ \frac{1}{2}(A - B)}\]

\[\mathrm{area} = \frac{be\ \sin\ A}{2} = \left[ {s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)} \right]^{\frac{1}{2}}\]

\[s = \frac{1}{2}(a + b + c)\]

#### 4.3.149 Formulas for Solution of Spherical Triangles

If \(A\), \(B\) and \(C\) are the three angles and \(a\), \(b\) and \(e\) the opposite sides,

\[\frac{\sin\ A}{\sin\ a} = \frac{\sin\ B}{\sin\ b} = \frac{\sin\ C}{\sin\ c}\]

\[\cos\ a = \cos\ b\ \cos\ e + \sin\ b\ \sin\ e\ \cos\ A\] \[= \frac{\cos\ b\ \cos\ (e \pm \theta)}{\cos\ \theta}\]

where tan \(\theta = \tan\ b\ \cos\ A\)

\[\cos\ A = - \cos\ B\ \cos\ C + \sin\ B\ \sin\ C\cos\ a\]

### Inverse Circular Functions Definitions

#### 4.4.1 Definitions

\[\mathrm{arcsin}\ z = \int_{0}^{z}\frac{dt}{(1 - t^{2})^{\frac{1}{2}}}\ \ \ \ (z = x + iy)\]

